Notes and small observations:\par
- Input validation is minimal: the program accepts any character for the initial marker selection (line 70) and does not convert lowercase to uppercase or check validity (could be improved).\par
- checkWinner() returns current_player when it finds a three-in-a-row; this relies on the assumption that checkWinner() is called immediately after a move by the player to be considered the winner (which is true in this code).\par
- The program uses i-- and continue to allow the same player to retry after invalid input or choosing an occupied slot.\par
- The board stores characters '1'..'9' initially; after markers are placed, those are replaced by 'X' or 'O'.\par
